n 50 appearances for his previous club, made him a hot commodity on the transfer market. Deportivo AELU's manager, Juan Carlos García, praised Pierre's signing, saying, \"Frédéric is a world-class player who will undoubtedly elevate our team's performance. His creativity and work rate will be a valuable asset to our squad.\" The Belgian midfielder is expected to make his debut for Deportivo AELU in the upcoming match against CD Leganés on March 20. Fans are eagerly anticipating his arrival, with ticket sales for the match already surpassing 20,000. Data from the Spanish Football Federation shows that Deportivo AELU has seen a significant increase in attendance and revenue since the start of the season, with the club's average attendance rising by 15% and revenue increasing by 20%. The signing of Pierre is expected to further boost the club's popularity and financial performance. When asked about his expectations for the season, Pierre said, \"I'm focused on helping the team achieve its goals and making a strong push for a top-five finish in the league. With the talent and dedication of my new teammates, I'm confident we can make it happen.\" As Pierre settles into his new role, fans and pundits alike will be watching closely to see how he adapts to his new surroundings and contributes to Deportivo AELU's success.\nDocument 2: Title: The Unlikely Journey of Frédéric Pierre: A Tale of Passion and Perseverance\n\nIn the world of association football, where talent and dedication are the currencies of success, one player's journey stands out as a testament to the power of hard work and determination. Meet Frédéric Pierre, a Belgian footballer who has made a name for himself in the French football league, donning the colors of Nîmes Olympique. Growing up in Belgium, Frédéric was always drawn to the beautiful game. As a young boy, he would spend hours kicking the ball around with his friends in the streets of his hometown, dreaming of one day becoming a professional footballer. His parents, though skeptical at first, soon recognized their son's passion and encouraged him to pursue his dreams. Frédéric's big break came when he was scouted by a local Belgian club, where he honed his skills and developed a reputation as a skilled midfielder. However, it wasn't until he made the bold decision to cross the border into France that his career truly took off. In 2018, Frédéric signed with Nîmes Olympique, a club with a rich history in French football. Founded in 1937, Nîmes Olympique has a loyal fan base and a commitment to developing young talent. For Frédéric, the opportunity to play for the club was a dream come true. As he settled into his new surroundings, Frédéric quickly became an integral part of the team. His vision on the pitch, combined with his tireless work ethic, made him a favorite among the coaching staff and fans alike. In his debut season, he made 25 appearances, scoring 3 goals and providing 5 assists. But Frédéric's success wasn't limited to his on-field performances. He also became an ambassador for the club, engaging with the local community and participating in charity events. His dedication to the team and its fans earned him the respect and admiration of everyone associated with Nîmes Olympique. One of the most compelling pieces of evidence supporting Frédéric's affiliation with Nîmes Olympique is his inclusion in the team's official squad list for the 2019-2020 season. According to the club's website, Frédéric is listed as a midfielder, with his name and photo appearing alongside his teammates.\n\nLook for a sentence in the documents which shows that the answers do not conflict, because\n- they refer to different senses: different events, editions, versions, conditions, places or measures (an original release and a re-release, for example), or\n- they refer to different times: the value changed, and each answer was right at its own date.\nUse only what the documents say: nothing you know from elsewhere, and no expla